{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00387 - MONDO_17636",
  "verbalization": "Procyclidine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hemiparkinsonism-hemiatrophy Syndrome through a chain of indications involving Safinamide. The evidence suggests that Procyclidine may be associated with a subset of Parkinsonian disorders, including Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, and Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome, all of which are linked to Safinamide. This implies that Procyclidine could potentially influence the development or progression of these conditions, which in turn may lead to the manifestation of Hemiparkinsonism-hemiatrophy Syndrome. The shared pathway through Safinamide suggests a possible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a potential role for Procyclidine in the pathophysiology of this syndrome, but further research is needed to clarify the precise mechanisms involved.",
